# The contents of these example directories are .out files which are installed
# in /usr/share/Macaulay2/PackageName/examples and are used by Macaulay2's own
# help function to print example code.  For most packages, these .out files
# are generated during build, but for several packages, they are included
# in the source as they rely on 3rd party software which may or may not be
# available.  In particular:
# * AdjointIdeal, ConvexInterface, MapleInterface, Parametrization: maple
#   (proprietary)
# * Bertini: bertini (non-free license)
# * CoincidentRootLoci: qepcad (not in Debian, RFP #951553)
# * MonodromySolver, NumericalSchubertCalculus, PHCpack: phcpack (not in Debian,
#   ITP #820848)
# * NCAlgebra: bergman (not in Debian, license appears to be free)
# * StatePolytope, Tropical: polymake (in Debian, but upstream doesn't assume
#   it's available during build like it does gfan, 4ti2, nauty, etc.)
macaulay2 source: package-does-not-install-examples M2/Macaulay2/packages/AdjointIdeal/examples/
macaulay2 source: package-does-not-install-examples M2/Macaulay2/packages/Bertini/examples/
